course: dictionary
lesson: 6301
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them, their context, tell you which meaning is right. «Moray eels open and close their mouths to pump water over their gills» is about a fish, because eels, gills and water are clues.
explain: The word moray also names a place. Moray is an area in the north-east of Scotland, and the Moray Firth is a sea inlet there. If a sentence talks about Scotland, a firth or a map, it means the place. If it talks about reefs, teeth or hunting, it means the animal.
explain: Read the whole sentence before you decide. «Groupers shake their heads at moray eels to invite them to hunt together» tells you the eel is a sea creature that hunts. Test your meaning in the sentence: does "a long, snake-like fish with sharp teeth" fit? Yes, so that is the right meaning.
fact: A moray, or moray eel, is a long, snake-like fish with sharp teeth.
fact: Morays live in holes in coral reefs and rocks in warm seas.
fact: Morays open and close their mouths to pump water over their gills to breathe, so they can look scary but are not threatening.
fact: Moray is also the name of an area in the north-east of Scotland.
fact: The Moray Firth is a sea inlet in Scotland, famous for dolphins.
exercise: «Moray eels open and close their mouths to pump water over their gills.» What is a moray in this sentence? | An area in north-east Scotland | A kind of dolphin | A sea inlet | *A long, snake-like fish with sharp teeth
exercise: «The Moray Firth is a sea inlet famous for dolphins.» What does Moray mean in this sentence? | A coral reef | A type of dolphin | A fish with sharp teeth | *A place in north-east Scotland
exercise: Which word in «Groupers shake their heads at moray eels to invite them to hunt together» is a clue that the eel is an animal? | heads | together | invite | *hunt
test: Where is the Moray Firth? | *Sea inlet in north-east Scotland | Hole in a rock | Coral reef in warm seas | Deep cave under a mountain
test: Which is a true description of a moray eel? | *Long, snake-like fish with sharp teeth | Has no teeth at all | Lives in cold lakes | Short, round and sweet
exam: Why do moray eels open and close their mouths? | To threaten divers | To sing to other fish | *To pump water over their gills to breathe | To catch dolphins
